      ],
      "holdout_is_unsealed_at_probe_time": true,
      "parser_accepts_an_unsealed_2025_document": false,
      "raised": "UnexpectedResponse",
      "message": "c17 preflight synthetic A65 probe: response contains timestamps in SEALED year(s) [2025]. ENTSO-E's periodEnd is meant to be exclusive, so this must not happen; refusing to parse or cache it. See CLAUDE.md and data/holdout.py."
    },
    "tier_a_2025_pull_is_blocked": true,
    "diagnosis": {
      "where": "data/entsoe.py, in parse_document (the sealed-timestamp check)",
      "what": "the check compares the parsed frame's years against sealed_years() and raises UnexpectedResponse on a hit, without asking holdout_is_unsealed() whether the human has approved the unseal. sealed_years() is the permanent declaration in config/data.yaml and still reads {2025} by design, so after Checkpoint C the check refuses every 2025 response.",
      "why_it_was_right_before": "its stated purpose is to catch an inclusive periodEnd \u2014 a 2024 request coming back with 2025 rows. While 2025 was sealed, 'contains a sealed year' and 'leaked past the requested window' were the same condition.",
      "the_two_sibling_checks_that_are_correct": [
        "data/prices.py:120 \u2014 belt-and-braces, routes through assert_not_sealed",
        "data/exogenous.py:275 \u2014 belt-and-braces, routes through assert_not_sealed"
      ],
      "proposed_fix": "route the same hit through data.holdout.assert_not_sealed(hit, ...) instead of raising directly, matching the two sibling checks. assert_not_sealed applies the identical sealed-year test and then honours holdout_is_unsealed(), so the tripwire keeps working for every year that is still sealed and yields only to the human's approval.",
      "what_the_fix_does_not_lose": "the check never compared the response against the *requested* year, so it never guarded the exclusive-periodEnd property for an unsealed year. Nothing that was being checked stops being checked.",
      "why_this_cycle_did_not_apply_it": "it is a sealed-holdout assertion. CLAUDE.md makes editing a data-contract or leakage-assertion file a flag-and-stop event, and PLAN.md lists 'before modifying a frozen test/contract' as one of its five human checkpoints. An unattended cycle editing a seal tripwire, in the cycle that first touches the holdout, is the case those rules exist for.",
      "scope_of_the_consequence": {
        "blocked": [
          "gbm_load_only",
          "gbm_res_persistence",
          "lear_load_only",
          "lear_res_persistence"
        ],
        "not_blocked": [
          "the nine-zone headline comparable arm (LEAR price_only)",
          "the naive_last_week floor",
          "the perfect-foresight oracle ceiling",
          "every Tier-B arm",
          "the Tier-A price_only arms"
        ],
        "note": "the headline needs Energy-Charts prices only and is unaffected. It was nevertheless not run: see the PROGRESS.md entry for why a once-only holdout is evaluated whole or not at all."
      }
    }
  },
